{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#disability-services-coordinator": {
      "title": "Disability Services Coordinator",
      "description": "Disability Services Coordinator. AVAILABLE: Immediately. This is a full-time, benefit eligible position. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. SALARY/RANK: Commensurate with qualifications and experience. QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree in Counseling, Higher Education, Student Affairs, Social Work, Special Education, Rehabilitation Counseling, or a related field preferred. Professional licensure or certification in Counseling, Social Work, Rehabilitation Counseling, or a related field preferred. Relevant professional certifications in disability/accessibility services are desirable. 1- 3 years prior professional experience in disability services, accessibility services, academic support, student services, counseling, or a related field preferred. Experience working with college students and/or individuals with disabilities preferred. Capable of working independently, candidates should possess strong analytical, organizational and communication skills and have demonstrated ability to work collaboratively and effectively with various constituent groups. The successful candidate must demonstrate a strong Christian faith, a commitment to the University's Mission, and a demonstrated commitment to that faith, through his/her professional responsibilities, relationships and the mentoring of students. As a Christian University, Waynesburg University hires as full-time staff only persons who profess faith in Jesus Christ and demonstrate that faith in a manner consistent with the mission and institutional commitments of the University. RESPONSIBILITIES: Manage the operations of the Disability Services Office (DSO) and serve as the primary contact for students with disabilities who seek or receive accommodations. Coordinate the accommodation process from initial inquiry and documentation review through implementation, follow-up, and ongoing support. Gather and analyze data related to the DSO for use in student success reporting. Review and update DSO policies and procedures and maintain and update DSO content and resources on University’s website. Meets with prospective students and families who may have questions regarding accommodations. Assist in developing and organizing disability-focused programs, workshops, or events. Promote an accessible, inclusive, and supportive educational environment consistent with the mission and values of the University. THE UNIVERSITY: Waynesburg University is a Christian higher education institution offering undergraduate and graduate programs both on the Waynesburg Campus and in adult centers in the Pittsburgh region. Directed by its Christian values, the University provides opportunities for scholarship, leadership and service to all of our students through an academic foundation for life-long learning and compassionate contribution to others. Special care is taken to employ people who embody the values and perspectives of the institution in their teaching, their personal lives, and their relationships with students. Serving more than 1,100 students, the University is a member of the Association of Presbyterian Colleges and Universities (APCU). For further information on these organizations, please refer to their respective web pages. APPLICATION PROCESS: Candidates must submit a resume/cv, letter of interest, along with a written statement that articulates how the candidate intends to demonstrate his/her Christian faith through the Mission of the University, his/her professional responsibilities, relationships and the mentoring of students. Also include names/addresses/phone numbers of five references. Include transcripts (unofficial copies are acceptable initially). Apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 West College Street Waynesburg, PA 15370 (Email: hr@waynesburg.edu )"
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#maintenance-worker": {
      "title": "Maintenance Worker",
      "description": "Maintenance Worker. Waynesburg University is accepting applications for the position of Maintenance worker. This is a full-time position. Advanced knowledge of practices and work methods associated with building maintenance and grounds-keeping. Superior knowledge of carpentry, plumbing, painting, air conditioning, heating and electrical fields. Ability to operate University maintenance vehicles and tractors and a valid driving license required. Good working knowledge of tools and equipment used in maintenance, repair, and grounds-keeping fields. High school graduate or GED equivalency preferred. Ability to understand and follow written and oral instructions is essential. Apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 West College Street Waynesburg, PA 15370 (Email: hr@waynesburg.edu )"
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#financial-aid-secretary": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Secretary",
      "description": "Financial Aid Secretary. Waynesburg University is seeking a full-time Secretary position for the Financial Aid Office at the Waynesburg campus. Candidates must possess a high school degree or GED and three years of professional experience. Excellent computer and analytical skills, as well as the ability to work independently, exercise good judgment, and project a positive, client-friendly public image are all necessary. Previous work experience in a financial aid or higher education setting preferred. Excellent oral and written communication skills are required. Typical work schedule is Monday-Friday, 8:30 a.m.-4:00 p.m. Demonstrated ability to use computerized systems such as Microsoft Office and perform the duties in the Secretarial job description required. Apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 West College Street Waynesburg, PA 15370 (Email: hr@waynesburg.edu )"
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#collections-manager-special-collections-museum-curator": {
      "title": "Collections Manager/Special Collections Museum Curator",
      "description": "Collections Manager/Special Collections Museum Curator. AVAILABLE: Immediately. This is a full-time, benefit-eligible position. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. SALARY/RANK: Commensurate with qualifications and experience. QUALIFICATIONS: Master’s degree in Museum Studies, Library Science, Art History, Anthropology, History, or a related field with an emphasis in collections management preferred. Experience with NAGPRA compliance. One (1) year of hands-on experience in collections management, including preventive conservation and collections management database oversight. Detail-oriented with ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. The successful candidate must demonstrate a strong Christian faith, a commitment to the University's Mission, and a demonstrated commitment to that faith, through his/her professional responsibilities, relationships and the mentoring of students. RESPONSIBILITIES: The Collections Manager /Special Collections Museum Curator is responsible for managing, preserving, and interpreting rare and unique collections, including Native American collections, in accordance with professional museum standards and the Native American Graves Protection and Repatriation Act (NAGPRA). This role involves curation, research, and public engagement to ensure the collection's integrity and accessibility. Other responsibilities within the department may be assigned as needed. THE UNIVERSITY: Waynesburg University is a Christian higher education institution offering undergraduate and graduate programs both on the Waynesburg Campus and in adult centers in the Pittsburgh region. Directed by its Christian values, the University provides opportunities for scholarship, leadership and service to all of our students through an academic foundation for life-long learning and compassionate contribution to others. Special care is taken to employ people who embody the values and perspectives of the institution in their teaching, their personal lives, and their relationships with students. Serving more than 1,100 students, the University is a member of the Association of Presbyterian Colleges and Universities (APCU). For further information on these organizations, please refer to their respective web pages. APPLICATION PROCESS: Candidates must submit a resume/cv, letter of interest, along with a written statement that articulates how the candidate intends to demonstrate his/her Christian faith through the Mission of the University, his/her professional responsibilities, relationships and the mentoring of students. Also include names/addresses/phone numbers of five references. Include transcripts (unofficial copies are acceptable initially). Apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 West College Street Waynesburg, PA 15370 (Email: hr@waynesburg.edu )"
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#university-librarian": {
      "title": "University Librarian",
      "description": "University Librarian. AVAILABLE: Immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. This is a part-time, non-benefits eligible position. SALARY/RANK: Commensurate with qualifications and experience. QUALIFICATIONS: MLS or MLIS from an ALA-accredited program desired. Experience with cataloging and integrated library systems. Experience managing serials and interlibrary loan operations. Excellent organization, collaboration, and time-management skills. Commitment to student success and accessibility in library services. Professional cataloging experience in an academic or research library. Knowledge of book repair and preservation. Familiarity with electronic resource management systems. As a Christian University rooted in the Evangelical and Reformed tradition, Waynesburg University hires as full-time staff only persons who profess faith in Jesus Christ and demonstrate that faith in a manner consistent with the mission and institutional commitments of the University. RESPONSIBILITIES: The University Librarian (Part-Time) supports the academic mission of the institution by managing cataloging, serials, and interlibrary loan operations. This position ensures the accuracy, accessibility, and organization of library resources in all formats and provides leadership in maintaining bibliographic data and resource sharing through OCLC and related systems. The librarian works collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students to facilitate discovery and delivery of scholarly materials. The librarian will assist with developing up-to-date collections, creating related displays, and supporting library programming and initiatives. THE UNIVERSITY: Waynesburg University is a Christian higher education institution offering undergraduate and graduate programs both on the Waynesburg Campus and in adult centers in the Pittsburgh region. Directed by its Christian values, the University provides opportunities for scholarship, leadership and service to all of our students through an academic foundation for life-long learning and compassionate contribution to others. Special care is taken to employ people who embody the values and perspectives of the institution in their teaching, their personal lives, and their relationships with students. The University is guided by a sound strategic vision and has served as a leader in service-learning, technology applications and student-centered learning among higher education institutions. The Waynesburg campus is located one hour from Pittsburgh. Waynesburg University is a member of the Association of Presbyterian Colleges and Universities (APCU). APPLICATION PROCESS: Candidates must submit resume/cv and letter of interest, along with a written statement that articulates the relationship between the candidate's profession and his/her Christian faith, and names/addresses/phone numbers of five references. Include transcripts (unofficial copies are acceptable initially). Apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 West College Street Waynesburg, PA 15370 (Email: hr@waynesburg.edu )"
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#library-assistant": {
      "title": "Library Assistant",
      "description": "Library Assistant. AVAILABLE: Immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. This is a part-time, non-benefits eligible position. SALARY/RANK: Commensurate with qualifications and experience. QUALIFICATIONS: Experience with cataloging and library systems. Excellent organization, collaboration, and time-management skills. Commitment to student success and accessibility in library services. Professional cataloging experience in an academic or research library preferred. Familiarity with electronic resource management systems. MLS or MLIS from an ALA-accredited program preferred. As a Christian University rooted in the Evangelical and Reformed tradition, Waynesburg University hires as full-time staff only persons who profess faith in Jesus Christ and demonstrate that faith in a manner consistent with the mission and institutional commitments of the University. RESPONSIBILITIES: The Library Assistant (Part-Time) supports the academic mission of the institution by managing cataloging, serials, and interlibrary loan operations. This position ensures the accuracy, accessibility, and organization of library resources in all formats and provides leadership in maintaining bibliographic data and resource sharing through OCLC and related systems. The Library Assistant works collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students to facilitate discovery and delivery of scholarly materials. The assistant will support the development of up-to-date collections, create related displays, and engage in library programming and initiatives while supervising work-study students during at least two evening shifts per week. THE UNIVERSITY: Waynesburg University is a Christian higher education institution offering undergraduate and graduate programs both on the Waynesburg Campus and in adult centers in the Pittsburgh region. Directed by its Christian values, the University provides opportunities for scholarship, leadership and service to all of our students through an academic foundation for life-long learning and compassionate contribution to others. Special care is taken to employ people who embody the values and perspectives of the institution in their teaching, their personal lives, and their relationships with students. The University is guided by a sound strategic vision and has served as a leader in service-learning, technology applications and student-centered learning among higher education institutions. The Waynesburg campus is located one hour from Pittsburgh. Waynesburg University is a member of the Association of Presbyterian Colleges and Universities (APCU). APPLICATION PROCESS: Candidates must submit resume/cv and letter of interest, along with a written statement that articulates the relationship between the candidate's profession and his/her Christian faith, and names/addresses/phone numbers of five references. Include transcripts (unofficial copies are acceptable initially). Apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 West College Street Waynesburg, PA 15370 (Email: hr@waynesburg.edu )"
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#part-time-nursing-clinical-instructors-hybrid-programs": {
      "title": "Part-Time Nursing Clinical Instructors – Hybrid Programs",
      "description": "Part-Time Nursing Clinical Instructors – Hybrid Programs. The Waynesburg University Department of Nursing invites applications for part-time clinical instructors to support our growing hybrid nursing programs, including the LPN-to-BSN and Second-Degree BSN pathways. Clinical instructors will provide direct supervision, instruction, and evaluation of nursing students during weekend clinical rotations at healthcare facilities throughout the region. Opportunities are available in a variety of clinical areas based upon program needs and the instructor's area of expertise. This position is particularly well suited for practicing registered nurses who are interested in nursing education while maintaining their current clinical practice. Previous teaching experience is welcomed but is not required. Faculty support and orientation are provided to assist nurses who are new to clinical education. A master's degree in nursing is preferred. Candidates with a bachelor's degree in nursing who are currently enrolled in a master's degree program will be considered. Candidates must hold, or be eligible to obtain, a current nursing license and must be committed to the mission and purpose of Christian higher education. Applicants should submit a CV/resume, a letter of interest, and the names, addresses, email addresses, and phone numbers of three professional references. Application materials may be submitted in digital form to: Dr. Sherry Zak, Chair, Nursing Department, at szak@waynesburg.edu , or to the Human Resources Office at hr@waynesburg.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#housekeeper": {
      "title": "Housekeeper",
      "description": "Housekeeper. Waynesburg University is accepting applications for a Housekeeper position. This is a part-time position that will work 19 hours per week, and will be scheduled to work nights and weekends. Housekeepers are required to follow an established routine, perform cleaning functions designed to keep various University facilities clean and orderly. Duties include: sweeping, mopping, vacuuming, scrubbing, dusting, etc. High school graduate or GED equivalency preferred. Some experience in providing housekeeping or janitorial services required. A good working knowledge of tools and equipment used in housekeeping services preferred. Ability to understand and follow written and oral instructions is essential. Qualified applicants should apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 West College Street Waynesburg, PA 15370 (Email: hr@waynesburg.edu )"
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#center-for-politics-law-and-policy-program-coordinator": {
      "title": "Center for Politics, Law and Policy Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Center for Politics, Law and Policy Program Coordinator. Waynesburg University is seeking applicants for the position of Center for Politics Law and Policy Program Coordinator. This is a part-time, non-benefits eligible position. Associate degree or equivalent combination of education and relevant training and experience. Bachelor's degree in business administration, education, communications, event management, hospitality or a related field preferred. Experience in administrative support, program coordination, event planning, student services, higher education or a related area. Experience coordinating events, travel, purchasing, budgets, calendars and communications preferred. Coordinates and administers the activities, programs, events, travel, communications and operational needs associated with the Stover Scholar Program. Provides comprehensive administrative and programmatic support to ensure the effective planning and execution of activities, including academic, social, cultural and professional development opportunities. Maintains program records, processes financial and purchasing transactions, coordinates schedules and logistics, communicates with students and university personnel and oversees the program budget and related expenditures. Manages the Stover Center website and social media presence. Successful candidates must demonstrate a strong Christian faith, a commitment to the University’s mission and a demonstrated commitment to that faith, through his/her professional responsibilities, relationships and the mentoring of students. Send resume/CV and letter of interest, along and names, addresses and phone numbers of five references. Include transcripts (unofficial copies are acceptable initially). Apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 West College Street Waynesburg, PA 15370 (Email: hr@waynesburg.edu ) For further information, please see the University home page: www.waynesburg.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#theater-instructor": {
      "title": "Theater Instructor",
      "description": "Theater Instructor. POSITION AVAILABLE: The Fine Arts Department seeks applicants for a part-time instructor in Theater to teach courses in the Theater Program and to direct theater productions during the 2026-2027 academic year. A completed Master’s degree required, Doctorate in Theater or a related field preferred. Prior experience teaching in a university/college setting preferred. Candidates must be committed to the mission and purpose of Christian higher education. Candidates must submit a CV (resume), a letter of interest, and the names, addresses, e-mails, and phone numbers of three references to: Human Resources Office, Waynesburg University, 51 W. College St., Waynesburg, PA, 15370. Materials may be submitted in digital form to: hr@waynesburg.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#assistant-soccer-coach": {
      "title": "Assistant Soccer Coach",
      "description": "Assistant Soccer Coach. Waynesburg University is currently seeking applicants for a part-time Assistant Men’s Soccer Coach in its NCAA Division III soccer program, which is a member of the President’s Athletic Conference. Responsibilities for the position include coaching, recruiting and administration within the program. Other responsibilities within the athletic department may be assigned as needed. Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s degree preferred. Prior successful experience in coaching on a high school or intercollegiate level desired. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Successful candidates must demonstrate a strong Christian faith, a commitment to the University’s Mission and a demonstrated commitment to that faith, through his/her professional responsibilities, relationships and the mentoring of students. Send resume/cv and letter of interest, along with a written statement that articulates the relationship between the candidate’s profession and his/her Christian faith, and names/addresses/phone numbers of five references. Include transcripts (unofficial copies are acceptable initially). Apply to the Human Resources Office, Waynesburg University, 51 West College Street, Waynesburg, PA 15370, e-mail: hr@waynesburg.edu . For further information, please see the University home page at www.waynesburg.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#graduate-assistantship-athletics-women-s-basketball": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistantship - Athletics (Women's Basketball)",
      "description": "Graduate Assistantship - Athletics (Women's Basketball). Number of Positions: 1 Anticipated Dates: Position Available Summer 2026 Job Description: Waynesburg University Department of Athletics is seeking a graduate student to assist staff and coaches with the day-to-day operations of the department, specifically assigned to Women’s Basketball. Position entails working 19 hours a week in the Athletic Department. The graduate assistant will report to the Head Women’s Basketball Coach and Director of Athletics. Duties and responsibilities will include: Duties include: Recruit qualified student athletes to participate in the athletic program, as directed by the Head Women’s Basketball Coach Assist in the organization of practice sessions Work in accordance with all staff members of the Athletics Department and Waynesburg University Represent Waynesburg University Athletic Department in a positive manner Assist in the preparation of games Serve as site administrator for home athletic events out of season Comply with all rules affiliated with Waynesburg University, the Presidents’ Athletic Conference, and Division III of the NCAA Additional responsibilities as assigned by the Head Women’s Basketball Coach and/or Director of Athletics Job Qualifications: All interested candidates will need to successfully enroll in a graduate program at Waynesburg University in order to be eligible for the assistantship. Candidates must possess strong organizational, communication and computer skills, familiarity with a variety of software such as: Microsoft Office Suite, Photoshop, Adobe Professional, ARI, Slate, etc.; the ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment and meet established work deadlines; and availability to work evenings, Sundays and occasional weekends. Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Review of applications will begin immediately. Candidates must submit a resume and letter of interest, and a written statement that articulates how the candidate intends to incorporate the mission of the University with the requirements and function of the position. Also include the names, addresses, emails, and phone numbers of three references. Include transcripts (copies are acceptable initially). Apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 W. College St. Waynesburg, PA 15370 email: hr@waynesburg.edu"
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#graduate-assistantship-athletics": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistantship - Athletics",
      "description": "Graduate Assistantship - Athletics. Number of Positions: 1 Anticipated Dates: Position Available Summer 2026 Job Description: Waynesburg University Department of Athletics is seeking a graduate student to assist staff and coaches with the day-to-day operations of the department. Position entails working 19 hours a week in the Athletic Department. The graduate assistant will report to the Athletic Director. Duties and responsibilities will include: Duties include: Assist in the direction of assigned athletic teams Assist in the organization of practice sessions Positional or event coach, as needed Work in accordance with all staff members of the Athletics Department and Waynesburg University Represent Waynesburg University Athletic Department in a positive manner Recruit qualified student athletes to participate in the athletic program, as directed Work with the Admissions Office to schedule appointments for prospective student athletes, conduct tours as directed by the Admissions staff Conduct recruiting calls and mailings Assist in the preparation of game and practice sites Assist administration/staff in monitoring student athletes grades and activities Possess the ability to communicate the mission of the University and the goals of the Athletic Department to student athletes Demonstrate a commitment to the mission of the University Comply with all rules affiliated with Waynesburg University, the Presidents Athletic Conference, and Division III of the NCAA As directed, serve as an academic mentor and conduct academic workshops as directed Provide support for current student leadership programs and initiatives, including FCA and activities held in conjunction with Student Services. Additional responsibilities as assigned by the Athletic Director Job Qualifications: All interested candidates will need to successfully enroll in a graduate program at Waynesburg University in order to be eligible for the assistantship. Candidates must possess strong organizational, communication and computer skills, familiarity with a variety of software such as: Microsoft Office Suite, Photoshop, Adobe Professional, Front Rush, Slate, etc; the ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment and meet established work deadlines; and availability to work evenings, Sundays and occasional weekends. Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Review of applications will begin immediately. Candidates must submit a resume, letter of interest, and a written statement that articulates how the candidate intends to incorporate the mission of the University with the requirements and function of the position. Also include the names, addresses, emails, and phone numbers of three references. Include transcripts (copies are acceptable initially). Apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 W. College St. Waynesburg, PA 15370 email: hr@waynesburg.edu"
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#graduate-assistantship-athletics-baseball": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistantship - Athletics - Baseball",
      "description": "Graduate Assistantship - Athletics - Baseball. Number of Positions: 1 Anticipated Dates: Position Available Summer 2026 Job Description: Waynesburg University Department of Athletics is seeking a graduate student to assist staff and coaches with the day-to-day operations of the department, specifically assigned to Baseball. Position entails working 19 hours a week in the Athletic Department. The graduate assistant will report to the Head Baseball Coach and Director of Athletics. Duties and responsibilities will include: Duties include: Assist in the direction of assigned athletic teams Assist in the organization of practice sessions Work in accordance with all staff members of the Athletics Department and Waynesburg University Represent Waynesburg University Athletic Department in a positive manner Recruit qualified student athletes to participate in the athletic program, as directed by the Head Baseball Coach Assist in the preparation of game and practice sites Possess the ability to communicate the mission of the University and the goals of the Athletic Department to student-athletes Serve as site administrator for home athletic events out of season Comply with all rules affiliated with Waynesburg University, the Presidents’ Athletic Conference, and Division III of the NCAA Additional responsibilities as assigned by the Head Baseball Coach and/or Director of Athletics Job Qualifications: All interested candidates will need to successfully enroll in a graduate program at Waynesburg University in order to be eligible for the assistantship. Candidates must possess strong organizational, communication and computer skills, familiarity with a variety of software such as: Microsoft Office Suite, Photoshop, Adobe Professional, Front Rush, Slate, etc.; the ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment and meet established work deadlines; and availability to work evenings, Sundays and occasional weekends. Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Review of applications will begin immediately. Candidates must submit a resume and letter of interest, and a written statement that articulates how the candidate intends to incorporate the mission of the University with the requirements and function of the position. Also include the names, addresses, emails, and phone numbers of three references. Include transcripts (copies are acceptable initially). Apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 W. College St. Waynesburg, PA 15370 email: hr@waynesburg.edu"
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#graduate-assistantship-entrepreneurial-leadership-nest": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistantship – Entrepreneurial Leadership (Nest)",
      "description": "Graduate Assistantship – Entrepreneurial Leadership (Nest). Number of Positions: 1 Anticipated Dates: Position Available Summer 2026 Job Description: Waynesburg University Entrepreneurial Leadership Program is seeking a graduate student to assist staff with the day-to-day operations of the Nest. Position entails working 29 hours a week in the Nest. The graduate assistant will report to the Nest Director. Duties and responsibilities will include: Assist with general day-to-day office operation at the Nest Regularly staff the Nest and welcome guests during scheduled/unscheduled tours Provide various operational management of the Nest, including but not limited to: customer service, student staff management, online store management, social media, financial management and record keeping, new product development, and commencement assistance. Assistance with various eHIVE events and projects Assistance in supporting the three Learning Labs for the Entrepreneurial Leadership Program: The Nest, Makerspace & Project GROW All other duties to be assigned by the eHIVE Director & Chair of Entrepreneurial Leadership Job Qualifications: All interested candidates will need to successfully enroll in a graduate program at Waynesburg University in order to be eligible for the assistantship. This position requires attendance and staffing at eHIVE or Nest, which may include regular shifts during evening or weekend hours. This position requires the job seeker to be entrepreneurially minded, a self-starter, flexible, adaptable, and capable of working with little supervision. Strong communication skills are required. Professional and friendly customer service, leadership skills, and strong organizational skills are required for this position. Applicant must possess a valid driver’s license and the ability for passenger or good transport. Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Review of applications will begin immediately. Candidates must submit a resume and letter of interest, and a written statement that articulates how the candidate intends to incorporate the mission of the University with the requirements and function of the position. Also include the names, addresses, emails, and phone numbers of three references. Include transcripts (copies are acceptable initially). Apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 W. College St. Waynesburg, PA 15370 email: hr@waynesburg.edu"
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#graduate-assistantship-athletics-men-s-soccer": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistantship - Athletics - Men's Soccer",
      "description": "Graduate Assistantship - Athletics - Men's Soccer. Number of Positions: 1 Anticipated Dates: Position Available Summer 2026 Job Description: Waynesburg University Department of Athletics is seeking a graduate student to assist staff and coaches with the day-to-day operations of the department. Position entails working 19 hours a week in the Athletic Department. The graduate assistant will report to the Athletic Director. Duties and responsibilities will include: Duties include: Assist in the direction of assigned athletic teams Assist in the organization of practice sessions Positional or event coach, as needed Work in accordance with all staff members of the Athletics Department and Waynesburg University Represent Waynesburg University Athletic Department in a positive manner Recruit qualified student athletes to participate in the athletic program, as directed Work with the Admissions Office to schedule appointments for prospective student athletes, conduct tours as directed by the Admissions staff Conduct recruiting calls and mailings Assist in the preparation of game and practice sites Assist administration/staff in monitoring student athletes grades and activities Possess the ability to communicate the mission of the University and the goals of the Athletic Department to student athletes Demonstrate a commitment to the mission of the University Comply with all rules affiliated with Waynesburg University, the Presidents Athletic Conference, and Division III of the NCAA As directed, serve as an academic mentor and conduct academic workshops as directed Provide support for current student leadership programs and initiatives, including FCA and activities held in conjunction with Student Services Additional responsibilities as assigned by the Athletic Director Job Qualifications: All interested candidates will need to successfully enroll in a graduate program at Waynesburg University in order to be eligible for the assistantship. Candidates must possess strong organizational, communication and computer skills, familiarity with a variety of software such as: Microsoft Office Suite, Photoshop, Adobe Professional, Front Rush, Slate, etc.; the ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment and meet established work deadlines; and availability to work evenings, Sundays and occasional weekends. Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Review of applications will begin immediately. Candidates must submit a resume and letter of interest, a writing sample, and a written statement that articulates how the candidate intends to incorporate the mission of the University with the requirements and function of the position. Also include the names, addresses, emails, and phone numbers of three references. Include transcripts (copies are acceptable initially). Apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 W. College St. Waynesburg, PA 15370 email: HR@waynesburg.edu"
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#graduate-assistantship-athletics-esports": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistantship - Athletics - Esports",
      "description": "Graduate Assistantship - Athletics - Esports. Number of Positions: 1 Anticipated Dates: Position Available Spring/Summer 2026 Job Description: Waynesburg University Department of Athletics is seeking a graduate student, in the area of Esports, to assist with the recruitment and esports program development. Position entails working 19 hours per week. The graduate assistant will report to the Director of Athletics. Duties and responsibilities will include: Duties include: Assist the Director of Esports/Head Coach with the growth and implementation of the Esports Program Assist in the organization of practice sessions, onsite competitions, coordination of Esports events, etc. Game specific or event coach, as needed Work in accordance with all staff members of the Athletics Department, Admissions Office and Waynesburg University Represent Waynesburg University in a positive manner Recruit qualified student-athletes to participate in the Esports program, as directed Conduct recruiting calls and mailings Assist in the preparation of the Esports Arena for competitions, events, and practices Assist administration/staff in monitoring student-athletes academic progress Possess the ability to communicate the mission of the University and the goals of the Athletic Department to student-athletes Demonstrate a commitment to the mission of the University Comply with all rules affiliated with Waynesburg University and the NCAA, should the NCAA introduce Esports as an emerging sport Additional responsibilities as assigned by the Athletic Director. Job Qualifications: All interested candidates will need to successfully enroll in a graduate program at Waynesburg University in order to be eligible for the assistantship. Candidates must possess strong organizational, communication and computer skills, familiarity with a variety of software such as: Microsoft Office Suite, Photoshop, Adobe Professional, Front Rush, Slate, etc; the ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment and meet established work deadlines; and availability to work evenings, Sundays and occasional weekends. Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Review of applications will begin immediately. Candidates must submit a resume and letter of interest, a writing sample, and a written statement that articulates how the candidate intends to incorporate the mission of the University with the requirements and function of the position. Also include the names, addresses, emails, and phone numbers of three references. Include transcripts (copies are acceptable initially). Apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 W. College St. Waynesburg, PA 15370 email: HR@waynesburg.edu"
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#graduate-assistantship-public-safety-and-campus-security": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistantship – Public Safety and Campus Security",
      "description": "Graduate Assistantship – Public Safety and Campus Security. Number of Positions: 1 Anticipated Date: Immediately Job Description: Position entails working 19 hours a week for the Office of Public Safety . Tasks will be varied and diverse in nature, but all are related to the Public Safety. The graduate assistant will report to the Director of Public Safety. Duties include: Enforcing the laws of the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania all policies and procedures of Waynesburg University. Prevents criminal activity and protects property University-wide, including lots, buildings and surrounding areas. Controls traffic including the issuance of parking violations to ensure smooth flow of traffic. Routinely performs foot or mobile patrols to insure security of University or University lots, buildings and property. Assist individuals whose vehicles have become disabled Responds to emergency situations on campus and serves as a primary point of contact in the absence of the Director/Assistant Director of Public Safety. Provides directions and assistance to campus visitors. Provides escort service for students on an as needed basis for off campus doctor appointments, when Student Services/Health Services/Athletic Training Staff personnel are not available. Assists in evacuations during fire or bomb threats and provides emergency first aid in the event of injury. Assists outside law enforcement agencies in securing warrants on campus. Reports traffic, safety, or security infractions to proper authorities. Operation and use of telephones/cell phones. Assist with Event Staff operations. Support campus Emergency Operations. Job Qualifications: All interested candidates will need to successfully enroll in a graduate program at Waynesburg University in order to be eligible for the assistantship. This position requires the candidate to be a self-starter, and capable of working with little supervision, must possess strong organizational and communication skills; the ability to work independently and meet established work deadlines; and availability to work evenings, occasional weekends. Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Review of applications will begin immediately. Candidates must submit a resume and letter of interest, and a written statement that articulates how the candidate intends to demonstrate his/her Christian faith through 1.) The Mission of the University, 2.) Integrating faith and learning in the position, 3.) the mentoring of students. Also include the names, addresses, emails, and phone numbers of three references. Include transcripts (copies are acceptable initially). Apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 W. College St. Waynesburg, PA 15370 email: hr@waynesburg.edu"
    },
    "https://www.waynesburg.edu/careers#graduate-assistantship-athletics-men-s-women-s-wrestling": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistantship - Athletics - Men's & Women's Wrestling",
      "description": "Graduate Assistantship - Athletics - Men's & Women's Wrestling. Number of Positions: 1 Anticipated Dates: Position Available Summer 2024 Job Description: Waynesburg University Department of Athletics is seeking a graduate student to assist staff and coaches with the day-to-day operations of the department, specifically assigned to Men’s & Women’s Wrestling . Position entails working 19 hours a week in the Athletic Department. The graduate assistant will report to the Head Men’s & Women’s Wrestling Coaches and Director of Athletics. Duties and responsibilities will include: Duties include: Assist in the direction of assigned athletic teams Assist in the organization of practice sessions Work in accordance with all staff members of the Athletics Department and Waynesburg University Represent Waynesburg University Athletic Department in a positive manner Recruit qualified student athletes to participate in the athletic program, as directed by the Head Men’s & Women’s Wrestling Coaches Assist in the preparation of game and practice sites Possess the ability to communicate the mission of the University and the goals of the Athletic Department to student-athletes Serve as site administrator for home athletic events out of season Comply with all rules affiliated with Waynesburg University, the Presidents’ Athletic Conference, and Division III of the NCAA Additional responsibilities as assigned by the Head Men’s & Women’s Wrestling Coaches and/or Director of Athletics Job Qualifications: All interested candidates will need to successfully enroll in a graduate program at Waynesburg University in order to be eligible for the assistantship. Candidates must possess strong organizational, communication and computer skills, familiarity with a variety of software such as: Microsoft Office Suite, Photoshop, Adobe Professional, Front Rush, Slate, etc. ; the ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment and meet established work deadlines; and availability to work evenings, Sundays and occasional weekends. Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Review of applications will begin immediately. Candidates must submit a resume and letter of interest, and a written statement that articulates how the candidate intends to incorporate the mission of the University with the requirements and function of the position. Also include the names, addresses, emails, and phone numbers of three references. Include transcripts (copies are acceptable initially). Apply to: Human Resources Office Waynesburg University 51 W. College St. Waynesburg, PA 15370 email: HR@waynesburg.edu"
    }
  },
